Explanation of break: The break statement is used to exit the switch block immediately once a matching case is executed. Without break, execution continues sequentially into subsequent cases (fall-through).

Concept of Fall-through: When a matching case is found in a switch statement, execution begins at that case label and continues sequentially through all subsequent cases until a 'break' statement or the end of the switch block is encountered. This unintended or intended flow is called fall-through.

Code snippet demonstrating fall-through:
int day = 2;
