    case 1:
    case 2:
    case 3:
    case 4:
    case 5:
        System.out.println("Weekday");
        break;
    case 6:
    case 7:
        System.out.println("Weekend");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Invalid");
}

Explanation: Here fall-through is used intentionally to group multiple cases (1 to 5) to print 'Weekday' using a single statement block. It is prevented by placing a 'break' statement at the end of each case block.

